// The certified fragment has no streaming I/O, so cat.turp has no twin.
//
// cat.turp copies its input to its output byte by byte. A register machine
// takes its input before the run and yields one number at halt, so an echo
// that interleaves reading and writing cannot be expressed at all, however
// far the fragment is widened. This is a limit of the model rather than a
// missing feature, and it is why the bespoke compilers exist.
//
// The nearest thing the fragment can say is "how many bytes would have
// been copied", given the input in registers. That needs input variables;
// see docs/certified-compilation.md section 4b item 5.
var answer : int;
